Falsifies `memory_regions::proofs::coalescing_never_reclaims_a_held_page`.

The defect: the reclaim ignores whether a sibling is in flight. It reads as a simplification,
because the scan already found every live child, and the one region it misses is the one that
left the table at its claim and is still being revoked.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert!(after == watermark, "an in-flight sibling blocks the
reclaim")`, for any input that is not quiescent and has both floors under the watermark. In the
kernel that lowers the watermark under a sibling whose pages a peer may still map, and the next
split hands them out: the use-after-free §13 (capability revocation and untyped reclamation) exists to prevent.

diff --git a/crates/memory_regions/src/lib.rs b/crates/memory_regions/src/lib.rs
--- a/crates/memory_regions/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/memory_regions/src/lib.rs
@@ -143,7 +143,7 @@
 /// revoke finishes is the use-after-free. Never above `watermark`, so a floor that somehow
 /// exceeded it cannot hand out budget the parent never had.
 pub fn coalesced_watermark(watermark: u64, retyped_to: u64, live_to: u64, quiescent: bool) -> u64 {
-    if !quiescent {
+    if !quiescent && false {
         return watermark;
     }
     retyped_to.max(live_to).min(watermark)
